{"book":"II Kings","chapter":8,"entries":[{"id":9728,"title":"II Kings 8:1","segments":["¶Then spake Elisha unto the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, Arise, and go thou and thine household, and sojourn wheresoever thou canst sojourn: for the LORD hath called for a famine; and it shall also come upon the land seven years."],"ref":"II Kings 8:1","verse":1,"words":[{"text":"¶Then spake","strong":"H1696"},{"text":" Elisha","strong":"H477"},{"text":" unto the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":", whose son","strong":"H1121"},{"text":" he had restored to life","strong":"H2421"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Arise","strong":"H6965"},{"text":", and go","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" thou and thine household","strong":"H1004"},{"text":", and sojourn","strong":"H1481"},{"text":" wheresoever","strong":"H834"},{"text":" thou canst sojourn","strong":"H1481"},{"text":": for the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" hath called","strong":"H7121"},{"text":" for a famine","strong":"H7458"},{"text":"; and it shall also come","strong":"H935"},{"text":" upon the land","strong":"H776"},{"text":" seven","strong":"H7651"},{"text":" years","strong":"H8141"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9729,"title":"II Kings 8:2","segments":["And the woman arose, and did after the saying of the man of God: and she went with her household, and sojourned in the land of the Philistines seven years."],"ref":"II Kings 8:2","verse":2,"words":[{"text":"And the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":" arose","strong":"H6965"},{"text":", and did","strong":"H6213"},{"text":" after the saying","strong":"H1697"},{"text":" of the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":": and she went","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" with her household","strong":"H1004"},{"text":", and sojourned","strong":"H1481"},{"text":" in the land","strong":"H776"},{"text":" of the Philistines","strong":"H6430"},{"text":" seven","strong":"H7651"},{"text":" years","strong":"H8141"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9730,"title":"II Kings 8:3","segments":["And it came to pass at the seven years' end, that the woman returned out of the land of the Philistines: and she went forth to cry unto the king for her house and for her land."],"ref":"II Kings 8:3","verse":3,"words":[{"text":"And it came to pass at the seven","strong":"H7651"},{"text":" years","strong":"H8141"},{"text":"' end","strong":"H7097"},{"text":", that the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":" returned","strong":"H7725"},{"text":" out of the land","strong":"H776"},{"text":" of the Philistines","strong":"H6430"},{"text":": and she went forth","strong":"H3318"},{"text":" to cry","strong":"H6817"},{"text":" unto the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" for her house","strong":"H1004"},{"text":" and for her land","strong":"H7704"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9731,"title":"II Kings 8:4","segments":["And the king talked with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, Tell me, I pray thee, all the great things that Elisha hath done."],"ref":"II Kings 8:4","verse":4,"words":[{"text":"And the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" talked","strong":"H1696"},{"text":" with Gehazi","strong":"H1522"},{"text":" the servant","strong":"H5288"},{"text":" of the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Tell","strong":"H5608"},{"text":" me, I pray thee, all the great things","strong":"H1419"},{"text":" that Elisha","strong":"H477"},{"text":" hath done","strong":"H6213"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9732,"title":"II Kings 8:5","segments":["And it came to pass, as he was telling the king how he had restored a dead body to life, that, behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. And Gehazi said, My lord, O king, this [is] the woman, and this [is] her son, whom Elisha restored to life."],"ref":"II Kings 8:5","verse":5,"words":[{"text":"And it came to pass, as he was telling","strong":"H5608"},{"text":" the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" how he had restored","strong":"H2421"},{"text":" a dead body","strong":"H4191"},{"text":" to life","strong":"H2421"},{"text":", that, behold, the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":", whose son","strong":"H1121"},{"text":" he had restored to life","strong":"H2421"},{"text":", cried","strong":"H6817"},{"text":" to the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" for her house","strong":"H1004"},{"text":" and for her land","strong":"H7704"},{"text":". And Gehazi","strong":"H1522"},{"text":" said","strong":"H559"},{"text":", My lord","strong":"H113"},{"text":", O king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":", this [is] the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":", and this [is] her son","strong":"H1121"},{"text":", whom Elisha","strong":"H477"},{"text":" restored to life","strong":"H2421"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9733,"title":"II Kings 8:6","segments":["And when the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed unto her a certain officer, saying, Restore all that [was] hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now. {officer: or, eunuch}"],"ref":"II Kings 8:6","verse":6,"words":[{"text":"And when the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" asked","strong":"H7592"},{"text":" the woman","strong":"H802"},{"text":", she told","strong":"H5608"},{"text":" him. So the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" appointed","strong":"H5414"},{"text":" unto her a certain","strong":"H259"},{"text":" officer","strong":"H5631"},{"text":", saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Restore","strong":"H7725"},{"text":" all that [was] hers, and all the fruits","strong":"H8393"},{"text":" of the field","strong":"H7704"},{"text":" since the day","strong":"H3117"},{"text":" that she left","strong":"H5800"},{"text":" the land","strong":"H776"},{"text":", even until now. {officer: or, eunuch}"}]},{"id":9734,"title":"II Kings 8:7","segments":["¶And Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God is come hither."],"ref":"II Kings 8:7","verse":7,"words":[{"text":"¶And Elisha","strong":"H477"},{"text":" came","strong":"H935"},{"text":" to Damascus","strong":"H1834"},{"text":"; and Benhadad","strong":"H1130"},{"text":" the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" of Syria","strong":"H758"},{"text":" was sick","strong":"H2470"},{"text":"; and it was told","strong":"H5046"},{"text":" him, saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", The man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":" is come","strong":"H935"},{"text":" hither","strong":"H2008"},{"text":"."}]},{"id":9735,"title":"II Kings 8:8","segments":["And the king said unto Hazael, Take a present in thine hand, and go, meet the man of God, and enquire of the LORD by him, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?"],"ref":"II Kings 8:8","verse":8,"words":[{"text":"And the king","strong":"H4428"},{"text":" said","strong":"H559"},{"text":" unto Hazael","strong":"H2371"},{"text":", Take","strong":"H3947"},{"text":" a present","strong":"H4503"},{"text":" in thine hand","strong":"H3027"},{"text":", and go","strong":"H3212"},{"text":", meet","strong":"H7125"},{"text":" the man","strong":"H376"},{"text":" of God","strong":"H430"},{"text":", and enquire","strong":"H1875"},{"text":" of the LORD","strong":"H3068"},{"text":" by him, saying","strong":"H559"},{"text":", Shall I recover","strong":"H2421"},{"text":" of this disease","strong":"H2483"},{"text":"?"}]},{"id":9736,"title":"II Kings 8:9","segments":["So Hazael went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels' burden, and came and stood before him, and said, Thy son Benhadad king of Syria hath sent me to thee, saying, Shall I recover of this disease? {with...: Heb. in his hand}"],"ref":"II Kings 8:9","verse":9,"words":[{"text":"So Hazael","strong":"H2371"},{"text":" went","strong":"H3212"},{"text":" to meet","strong":"H7125"},{"text":" him, and took","strong":"H3947"},{"text":" a present","strong":"H4503"},{"text":" with him","strong":"H3027"},{"text":", even of every g